app's own code.

- libffmpegJNI.so, from io.put:media3-ffmpeg-decoder (Apache-2.0): FFmpeg,
  LGPL-2.1-or-later, built without --enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree and
  --enable-version3. The FFmpeg source that was built and the commands to
  rebuild and relink it are published next to each release on Maven Central
  as media3-ffmpeg-decoder-<version>-ffmpeg-source.tar.xz.
- libass.so, from io.github.peerless2012:ass-media (MIT): libass (ISC),
  FriBidi (LGPL-2.1-or-later), FreeType (FTL), HarfBuzz (MIT), fontconfig
  (HPND), libunibreak (Zlib) and Expat (MIT). Its source, with every library
  it links, is the libass-android tag the app pins, with its libass-cmake
  submodule.
- libsentry.so, from io.sentry:sentry-android-ndk: sentry-native (MIT).

Versions, copyrights, sources and licence texts for each are listed in the
app under Open source licenses, from playbackNotices and telemetryNotices.
